Unit tests (PlatformIO / Unity). Which env runs which suite is set in platformio.ini (test_ignore,
test_filter; tools/ci/test_lists.py checks that they agree), and CLAUDE.md "Build & verify" has the
commands. The lists in platformio.ini are the truth; this file only says what each env is for:

  pio test -e native-test              test_replay_corpus: recorded captures through the real detection chain
  pio test -e native-test-behavior     the host unit suites: each includes the src/ files it tests itself,
                                       no src build (test_filter in platformio.ini)
  pio test -e native-test-diag         test_detection_diagnostics (ANALYZER_MODE side channel)
  on-device (upload --without-testing, then reset and read the port):
                                       test_analyzer_pass_rules, test_timebase, test_shipped_profile
                                       (they also run in native-test-behavior, so host and board answer the
                                       same cases)

A new suite goes into one native env's test_filter and every ESP env's test_ignore, unless it is on-device
(tools/ci/test_lists.py ON_DEVICE).

Fixtures: test/fixtures (RAW captures, see test_replay_corpus/test_main.cpp for their provenance).
native_shim/Arduino.h stands in for <Arduino.h> on the host.
